{%- comment -%}
  Which storefront this visitor is on, answered ONCE for everything that
  reports it: the cart stamp in layout/theme.liquid and the three signup
  forms (popup-signup, waitlist-modal, footer).

  There were four copies of this, and they did not agree. The cart stamp
  treats the URL as the ground truth and falls back to routes.root_url;
  the three forms trusted routes.root_url alone. So on any page where that
  value fails to carry the market prefix, a signup reported market
  'primary', language 'en' and no path — a German shopper filed as an
  international one, with nothing on the record to say otherwise.

  window.STMarket() is that answer:

    { market: 'de', language: 'en', path: '/en-de' }
    { market: 'primary', language: 'en', path: '' }   ← the bare domain

  PATH is '' and not '/' on the primary market so Brevo templates can build
  URLs as domain + PATH + /page for every contact, and MARKET is what tells
  a bare-domain visitor from one nothing recorded — never the path.

  Chinese ships as zh-TW/zh-CN while our copy and every campaign branch are
  keyed by the bare code, so both collapse onto 'zh'.

  It is rendered in the head, before any section that calls it.

  What this CANNOT reach: the popup's own targeting, which picks the
  version to show in Liquid at render time from the same routes.root_url.
  Where that value is wrong the visitor sees the wrong popup, and no script
  running afterwards can undo it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  window.STMarket = window.STMarket || function () {
    /* The URL the visitor is on is the ground truth. routes.root_url
       normally matches it, but where it fails to reflect the market prefix
       the answer would silently read as the primary market, so a prefix in
       the path wins over the Liquid value. */
    var path = {{ routes.root_url | json }};
    if (path === '/') path = '';
    var seg = (window.location.pathname.split('/')[1] || '').toLowerCase();
    if (/^[a-z]{2}-[a-z0-9]{2,}$/.test(seg)) path = '/' + seg;

    var market = 'primary';
    if (path) {
      var segs = path.replace(/^\//, '').split('-');
      market = segs[segs.length - 1].toLowerCase();
    }
    var language = {{ localization.language.iso_code | downcase | split: '-' | first | json }};
    if (path) {
      var lseg = path.replace(/^\//, '').split('-')[0];
      if (lseg) language = lseg;
    }
    return { market: market, language: language, path: path };
  };
</script>
